# nr-office-comrs-word-read: the Word reader of mixdog-office-com (src/word/{mod,reading,snapshot,styles,selection,issues}.rs, the empty
# stub src/word/edit/mod.rs), tests/word_read.rs, tests/word_read_live.rs and recorder/scenarios/word-read.json.
# Nothing was compiled (the lead builds the wave); every file was checked to parse with rustfmt only.
# No protocol row, no service, no SERVICE_PENDING name and no Cargo.lock change belong to this task (it uses `regex`, already a dependency of the crate).

## 1. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/src/lib.rs (not owned by this task)
Add to the `pub mod` block (after `pub mod template;`):

    pub mod word;

## 2. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/src/drivers.rs (not owned by this task)
Fill the readers table:

    static READERS: &[(&str, &dyn FormatReader)] = &[("docx", &crate::word::Reader)];

(`EDITORS` stays empty: nr-office-comrs-word-edit adds `("docx", &crate::word::Editor)` and takes over `src/word/edit/mod.rs`, which this task
leaves as an empty module declared as `pub(crate) mod edit;` from word/mod.rs. The editor needs no edit of any file of this task: the style map
(`word::styles::canonical_style_name`, thread-local as `$script:WordLocalStyleMap` was per host) and the casts in word/mod.rs are reachable from
`word::edit` as `super::...` and `super::styles::...`.)

## 3. native/core/crates/mixdog-office-com/Cargo.toml (not owned by this task)
Test targets, after `[[test]] name = "actions_live"`:

    [[test]]
    name = "word_read"
    path = "tests/word_read.rs"

    [[test]]
    name = "word_read_live"
    path = "tests/word_read_live.rs"

## 4. What the lead should know
- `tests/word_read.rs` runs against a scripted Word object model written from the PowerShell source; `tests/fixtures/word-read/` does not exist yet
  because no recording could be made here (no Word): run `node recorder/record-office-com.mjs --area word-read` on the migration PC, then the
  call logs of the recorded snapshot and issues requests are to be replayed against `Reader` (the test file has the manifest check for them; the replay
  itself is not written, since the recorded steps' format has no sample in the tree yet).
- The order the document is asked for each built-in style's local name (`word/styles.rs`, `BUILTIN_STYLE_IDS`) is the enumeration order of
  the 36-key hashtable `$script:WordBuiltinStyleIds` as Windows PowerShell 5.1 lists it (observed in review by enumerating the script's
  hashtable in powershell.exe).
